  "id": "moog.dfam",
  "maker": "Moog",
  "model": "DFAM",
  "category": "semi-modular",
  "summary": "Drummer From Another Mother: a semi-modular percussion synthesiser with two oscillators, a noise source, two 8-step sequencers for pitch and velocity, and a 24-point patch bay. Normalled, so it makes sound with nothing patched. This entry sketches the patch bay rather than reproducing all 24 points. The panel is drawn at the arrangement - patch bay over the right, voice on the left, the two eight-step sequencer rows along the bottom. Both eight-step rows move: pitch and velocity, sixteen sliders. The entry still sketches the patch bay rather than reproducing all twenty-four points, which is a claim about sockets and not about controls.",
